-.
Executes an external program
Simple usage: .<program name>

[@] .GAME
Executes the GAME application
-ENDCOMMAND

-ABOUT
Shows basic information about the system.
Simple usage: ABOUT
-ENDCOMMAND

-APLIC
Displays and runs the applications installed on the system
Simple usage: APLIC

[@] APLIC
Run the APLIC command

[@] APLIC KISS
Run the KISS application
-ENDCOMMAND

-CAL
Displays a real-time calendar.
Simple usage: CAL [month] [year]  or  CAL <year>

[@] CAL
Opens the current month's calendar

[@] CAL 8
Opens the calendar for August of the current year

[@] CAL 2026
Opens the full calendar for the year 2026

[@] CAL 8 2026
Opens the calendar for August 2026
-ENDCOMMAND

-CD
Enters a directory. Supports paths with spaces.
Simple usage: CD <directory name>

[@] CD TEMP
Enters the TEMP directory

[@] CD "My Documents"
Enters a directory with a space in the name

[@] CD..
Leaves a directory

[@] CD\
Returns to the root directory
-ENDCOMMAND

-CLS
Clears the screen.
Simple usage: CLS
-ENDCOMMAND

-CLEAR
Clears the screen.
Simple usage: CLEAR

[@] CLEAR
Clears the screen like CLS
-ENDCOMMAND

-COLOR
Chooses the background and foreground colors for OSB.
Simple usage: COLOR
-ENDCOMMAND

-CONFIG
Makes changes to the basic PC configuration.
Simple usage: CONFIG

[@] CONFIG
1 - Boot message
2 - Prompt layout
0 - Exit
-ENDCOMMAND

-COPY
Copies files, with wildcard support.
Simple usage: COPY <source> <destination>

[@] COPY ARQUIVO.TXT BACKUP.TXT
Copies ARQUIVO.TXT to BACKUP.TXT

[@] COPY *.TXT C:\BACKUP
Copies all .TXT files to the C:\BACKUP directory
-ENDCOMMAND

-DATE
Displays the system date.
Simple usage: DATE
-ENDCOMMAND

-DEL
Deletes files from disk.
Simple usage: DEL [/S] <mask>

[@] DEL ARQUIVO.ARQ
Deletes a file

[@] DEL *.TMP
Deletes all .TMP files

[@] DEL /S *.TMP
Deletes all .TMP files recursively
-ENDCOMMAND

-DIR
Displays files and directories, with support for filters and paths with spaces.
Simple usage: DIR [path] [/W] [filter]

[@] DIR
Lists the current directory

[@] DIR C:\MEUS ARQUIVOS
Lists a directory with a space in the name

[@] DIR *.TXT
Lists only .TXT files

[@] DIR /W *.COM
Lists only .COM files in wide format
-ENDCOMMAND

-EXIT
Ends the OSB session.
Simple usage: EXIT
-ENDCOMMAND

-GAMES
Displays and runs the games installed on the system
Simple usage: GAMES

[@] GAMES
Run the GAMES command

[@] GAMES HANGMAN
Run the HANGMAN game
-ENDCOMMAND

-HELP
 -HELP
Available commands:

 You can chain multiple commands on the same line using the ';' separator (ex: DIR ; VER)

 . = Executes an MS-DOS or OSB program
ABOUT = About OSB
APLIC = Shows the applications included with OSB
CAL = Simple calendar
CD = Enter a directory (supports spaces)
CLS = Clear the screen
COLOR = Change the screen color
CONFIG = Operating system and PC settings
COPY = Copy files with wildcard support
DATE = Display the date
DEL = Delete files
DIR = Shows files in a directory (with filters)
EXIT = End the session
FIND = Search files by name or content
GAMES = Shows the games included with OSB
HELP = Help menu
KISS = Text-mode file editor
TOUR = Step-by-step tour of OSB
TODO = Task manager
MD = Create a directory (supports spaces)
MOVE = Move files from one location to another
OSL = Executes OSLANG 0.41 programs
PRINT = Print a file
PROMPT = Customize the prompt layout
PWD = Display the current directory
RD = Remove an empty directory
REN = Rename files with wildcard support
SET = Manage environment variables
SIZE = Display the size of a file
TIME = Display the time
TYPE = Show the contents of a file
USER = Manage users and authentication
 VER = Display the system version
 -ENDCOMMAND

-KISS
Edits a text file with line numbering and syntax highlighting for .osl files
Simple usage: KISS <file name>

[@] KISS C:\Carta.txt
Opens C:\Carta.txt with line numbers and, if it's .osl, OSLANG syntax highlighting
-ENDCOMMAND

-MD
Creates a directory. Supports names with spaces.
Simple usage: MD [/P] <directory name>

[@] MD TEMP
-ENDCOMMAND

[@] MD "MEUS ARQUIVOS"
Creates a directory with a space in the name

[@] MD /P C:\A\B\C
Creates the C:\A\B\C directory and all necessary parent directories
-ENDCOMMAND

-PRINT
Prints the contents of a file or evaluates a mathematical expression.
Simple usage: PRINT <file> | <expression>

[@] PRINT CARTA.TXT
Prints the contents of CARTA.TXT

[@] PRINT 2+2
Displays: 4

[@] PRINT 10*5+3
Displays: 53

[@] PRINT %VARIAVEL%
Displays the value of the variable
-ENDCOMMAND

-PROMPT
Customizes the OSB prompt layout.
Simple usage: PROMPT <layout>

Placeholders:
  %user      - Name of the authenticated user (or guest)
  %hostname  - Machine name
  %pwd       - Current directory
  %d         - Current date (dd/MM/yyyy)
  %t         - Current time (HH:mm:ss)
  %br        - Line break

[@] PROMPT %user@%hostname [@] %pwd
Changes the prompt to show user, machine, and directory
-ENDCOMMAND

-MOVE
Moves a file from one location to another.
Simple usage: MOVE <source> <destination>

[@] MOVE ARQUIVO.TXT C:\BACKUP\ARQUIVO.TXT
Moves the file to the backup directory

[@] MOVE CARTA.TXT C:\DOCS\
Moves the file to the DOCS directory
-ENDCOMMAND

-FIND
Searches for files by name or content.
Simple usage: FIND <text> [mask]

[@] FIND "ola"
Searches for "ola" in all files, recursively

[@] FIND "ola" *.osl
Searches for "ola" only in .osl files

[@] FIND /F "*.txt"
Lists all .txt files, recursively
-ENDCOMMAND

-SET
Manages environment variables.
Simple usage: SET [name=value]

[@] SET NOME=Ygor
Sets the NOME variable to Ygor

[@] SET NOME
Shows the value of the NOME variable

[@] SET NOME=
Removes the NOME variable

[@] SET
Lists all defined variables
-ENDCOMMAND

-PROMPT
Customizes the OSB prompt layout.
Available placeholders:
  %user      - Name of the authenticated user (or guest)
  %hostname  - Machine name
  %pwd       - Current directory
  %d         - Current date (dd/MM/yyyy)
  %t         - Current time (HH:mm:ss)
  %br        - Line break

[@] CONFIG
2 - Prompt layout
Enter the new layout, for example: %user@%hostname [@] %pwd
-ENDCOMMAND

 -RD
 Deletes an empty directory.
 Simple usage: RD <directory name>

 [@] RD TEMP
 -ENDCOMMAND

 -RECOVER
 Recovers a file or directory from the trash (.trash folder).
 Simple usage: RECOVER <file or directory name>

 [@] RECOVER TEXTO.TXT
 Recovers TEXTO.TXT from .trash to the current directory

 [@] RECOVER MEUPASTA
 Recovers MEUPASTA directory from .trash to the current directory
 -ENDCOMMAND

 -REN
Renames one or more files, with wildcard support.
Simple usage: REN <old name> <new name>

[@] REN TEXTO.TXT CARTA.TXT
Renames TEXTO.TXT to CARTA.TXT

[@] REN *.TXT *.DOC
Renames all .TXT files to .DOC
-ENDCOMMAND

-SIZE
Returns the size of a file (in Kbytes).
Simple usage: SIZE <file name>

[@] SIZE ARQUIVO.DOC
625 Kbytes
-ENDCOMMAND

-TIME
Displays the system time.
Simple usage: TIME
-ENDCOMMAND

-TOUR
Step-by-step tour of OSB.
Simple usage: APLIC TOUR

[@] APLIC TOUR
Runs the interactive system tour
-ENDCOMMAND

-TODO
Task manager.
Simple usage: TODO [ADD|LIST|DONE|CLEAR] <args>

[@] TODO ADD "comprar leite"
Adds a task

[@] TODO LIST
Lists only pending tasks

[@] TODO LIST ALL
Lists all tasks (pending and completed)

[@] TODO DONE 1
Marks task 1 as completed (adds [x])

[@] TODO CLEAR
Removes all tasks
-ENDCOMMAND

-TYPE
Displays the contents of a file.
Simple usage: TYPE <file name> [/P] [/P:N] [/N]

[@] TYPE ARQUIVO.TXT
This is the content of ARQUIVO.TXT

[@] TYPE ARQUIVO.TXT /N
Displays the content with line numbers

[@] TYPE ARQUIVO.TXT /P
Displays the content with a pause every 20 lines

[@] TYPE ARQUIVO.TXT /P:10
Displays the content with a pause every 10 lines

[@] TYPE SCRIPT.OSL
Displays the content with OSLANG syntax highlighting
-ENDCOMMAND

-VER
Displays the Operating System version.
Simple usage: VER
-ENDCOMMAND

-PWD
Displays the full path of the current directory.
Simple usage: PWD

[@] PWD
Displays the current directory.
-ENDCOMMAND

-HOSTNAME
Shows or changes the machine name.
Simple usage: HOSTNAME

[@] HOSTNAME
Displays the current machine name.

[@] HOSTNAME MEUMAC
Changes the machine name to MEUMAC.
-ENDCOMMAND

-USER
Manages users and authentication.
Simple usage: USER

[@] USER
Prompts for username and password to authenticate.

[@] USER ADD <name> <password>
Adds a new user.

[@] USER CHANGE <name> <password>
Changes the password of an existing user.

[@] USER DEL <name>
Removes an existing user.
-ENDCOMMAND

-HISTORY
Lists the command history, numbered, with date and time, and asks if you want to repeat any.
Simple usage: HISTORY [number]

[@] HISTORY
     1  2026-08-14 02:37:00  CD TEMP
     2  2026-08-14 02:38:00  DIR /W
     3  2026-08-14 02:39:00  VER
Repeat which number (ENTER for none)? 2
DIR /W

The history is saved per user in CONF\HISTORY\<user>.txt and is loaded again every time
OSB starts (stores the 1000 most recent commands).
-ENDCOMMAND

-GREP
Filters lines of text by a pattern (case-insensitive).
Simple usage: COMMAND ; GREP <pattern>

[@] DIR ; GREP git
Lists only files/folders containing "git"

[@] HISTORY ; GREP DIR
Lists only history commands containing "DIR"

[@] TYPE ARQ.TXT ; GREP erro
Displays only lines from the file containing "erro"
-ENDCOMMAND

-OSL
Executes a program written in OSLANG 0.4, the OSB scripting language.
Simple usage: OSL <file.osl>

[@] OSL FIBONACCI.OSL
Executes the FIBONACCI.OSL script

 [@] HELP OSL
 Shows this help

OSLANG 0.4 is OSB's programming language. It combines the simplicity of BASIC
with modern object-oriented features. This help summarizes the basic syntax.
For the complete specification, see OSLANG-0.4-SPEC.MD.

--- TYPES ---
NUMBER   Real numbers (ex: 3.14159, -10, 0)
STRING   Text in quotes (ex: "Hello World")
BOOLEAN  TRUE or FALSE
NULL     Null value (absence of value)
ARRAY    List of values (ex: [1, 2, 3])

--- VARIABLES ---
VAR Name NUMBER       Declares a NUMBER variable
VAR Name STRING       Declares a STRING variable
Name = 10             Assigns a value (implicitly declared)
Name = NULL           Assigns NULL (does not break type)

--- FUNCTIONS ---
FUNCTION NAME(parameters)
    commands
    RETURN value
END FUNCTION

Example:
FUNCTION SOMAR(A, B)
    RETURN A + B
END FUNCTION

--- OUTPUT ---
PRINT "Hello"                    Displays text
PRINT Name                       Displays variable
PRINT A + ": " + B               Concatenates with +

--- INPUT ---
INPUT Name                       Reads text from user

--- CONDITIONALS ---
IF condition THEN
    commands
END

IF condition THEN
    commands
ELIF other_condition THEN
    commands
ELSE
    commands
END

--- LOOPS ---
FOR I = 1 TO 10
    commands
END

WHILE condition
    commands
END

DO WHILE condition
    commands
END

--- TRY/CATCH ---
TRY
    commands
CATCH ERR
    PRINT "Error: " + ERR
END

--- STANDARD FUNCTIONS ---
STR(x)           Converts to STRING
NUMBER(x)        Converts to NUMBER
BOOL(x)          Converts to BOOLEAN
COUNT(arr)       Number of elements
TYPEOF(x)        Value type (STRING, NUMBER, BOOLEAN, ARRAY, NULL, or class name)

--- NAMESPACES (OSLANG 0.4) ---
MATH.SQRT(x)          Square root
MATH.ABS(x)           Absolute value
MATH.POW(base, exp)   Power
MATH.FLOOR(x)         Rounds down
MATH.CEIL(x)          Rounds up
MATH.RANDOM(min, max) Random integer
MATH.PI               PI constant
MATH.E                Euler's constant

FILE.READ(path)       Reads file as ARRAY of STRING (one line per element)
FILE.READTEXT(path)   Reads file as STRING
FILE.WRITE(path, text) Writes text to file
FILE.EXISTS(path)     Checks if file exists (BOOLEAN)
FILE.DELETE(path)     Deletes a file

DIR.LIST(path)        Lists files and folders as ARRAY of STRING
DIR.FILES(path)       Lists only files as ARRAY of STRING
DIR.DIRS(path)        Lists only folders as ARRAY of STRING
DIR.CURRENT()         Current directory as STRING
DIR.CHANGE(path)      Changes the current directory

--- PRIMITIVE METHODS (OSLANG 0.4) ---
Name.TOUPPER()        Converts string to uppercase
Name.TOLOWER()        Converts string to lowercase
Name.TRIM()           Removes extra spaces
Name.SUBSTR(i, len)   Extracts substring
Name.CONTAINS(text)   Checks if it contains text
Name.INDEXOF(text)    Text position (-1 if not found)
Name.LENGTH()         String length

Value.BETWEEN(a, b)   Checks if number is between a and b
Value.TOSTRING()      Converts number to string

Array.COUNT()         Number of elements
Array.FIRST()         First element
Array.LAST()          Last element
Array.CONTAINS(x)     Checks if it contains value
Array.MAP(fn)         Applies function to each element
Array.FILTER(fn)      Filters elements by function
Array.REDUCE(fn, init) Reduces array to a value

--- CLASSES AND OBJECTS (OSLANG 0.4) ---
CLASS Name
    members
END

INTERFACE Name
    members
END

--- PROPERTIES ---
VAR Name STRING       Class property
PRIVATE VAR Name      Restricted access
PROTECTED VAR Name    Access for class and derived classes
PUBLIC VAR Name       Free access (default)

--- METHODS ---
NAME(parameters)
    commands
    RETURN value
END

Example:
CLASS Calculadora
    PUBLIC SOMAR(A, B)
        RETURN A + B
    END
END

--- CONSTRUCTORS ---
CONSTRUCTOR(parameters)
    commands
END

Example:
CLASS Pessoa
    VAR Nome STRING
    
    CONSTRUCTOR(Nome STRING)
        ME.Nome = Nome
    END
END

--- INHERITANCE ---
CLASS Filho: Pai
    members
END

Example:
CLASS Animal
    VAR Nome STRING
    CONSTRUCTOR(Nome STRING)
        ME.Nome = Nome
    END
END

CLASS Cachorro: Animal
    CONSTRUCTOR(Nome STRING)
        BASE(Nome)
        commands
    END
END

--- INTERFACES ---
INTERFACE ICor
    GET()
    SET(Cor STRING)
END

CLASS Item: ICor
    PUBLIC GET()
        RETURN ME.Cor
    END
    PUBLIC SET(Cor STRING)
        ME.Cor = Cor
    END
END

--- ME ---
ME references the current object (equivalent to THIS in other languages)

Example:
CLASS Pessoa
    VAR Nome STRING
    PUBLIC GET_NOME()
        RETURN ME.Nome
    END
END

--- NEW ---
Object = NEW Class(args)

Example:
Pessoa = NEW Pessoa("Ygor")
PRINT Pessoa.GET_NOME()

--- VISIBILITY ---
PUBLIC      Access from anywhere
PROTECTED   Access in class and derived classes
PRIVATE     Access only in the declaring class

--- SHORTCUTS ---
<TAB>          Autocompletes commands and files
↑↓             Command history
←→             Edit current line
 ;              Executes multiple commands
 -ENDCOMMAND
